# Build context of the v2 image (the root Dockerfile), as an allowlist: exclude everything, then
# re-include only what the Dockerfile copies. Secrets (.env, tfvars), v1 code, infra, docs, local
# virtualenvs, node_modules and build output therefore never leave the machine.
#
# Two implementations read this file: `az acr build` applies it itself before uploading the
# context, and Docker/BuildKit applies it in CI. The Azure CLI's matcher is simpler than Docker's,
# so every rule stays in the subset both read the same way: no leading or trailing "/" on any line,
# "**" only as a whole path segment, and every "!" exception spelled from the repository root.
# Exclusions that refine a re-included tree come after it (the last matching line wins).
#
# v1 note: Dockerfile.webapp and Dockerfile.dev-* build from the repository root and need
# backend/ and frontend/, which this file excludes. To rebuild v1 before cutover, add an empty
# <name>.dockerignore next to that Dockerfile (both az acr build and BuildKit prefer it).
*

# Server: dependency manifests (the cached layer), the readme the wheel build needs, the package.
!server/pyproject.toml
!server/uv.lock
!server/README.md
!server/src

# Mermaid browser bundle for the renderer (npm ci in a build stage).
!server/vendor/package.json
!server/vendor/package-lock.json

# Web app: sources and configs. Dependencies and build output are excluded again below.
!web

# The contract files the server reads at runtime (blogwriter.publish.contract).
!contracts/published-blogs.v2.schema.json
!contracts/sanitizer-profile.json

# Local state inside the re-included trees.
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/coverage
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
web/.env*
web/*.local
web/*.tsbuildinfo
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
